solution:
Note that \begin{align*}
f(0) &= a(0)^2+b(0)+c \\
&=c
\end{align*}and \begin{align*}
f(1) &= a(1)^2+b(1)+c \\
&=a+b+c.
\end{align*}Thus, \begin{align*}
a+b+2c &= c + (a+b+c) \\
&= f(0)+f(1).
\end{align*}The graph of $y=f(x)$ passes through $(0,7)$ and $(1,4)$, so $f(0)=7$ and $f(1)=4$. Therefore, $a+b+2c = 7 + 4 = \boxed{11}$.

We simplify, bearing in mind that $i^2 = -1$. We get  \begin{align*}
(4-5i)(-5+5i) &= 4(-5) + 4(5i) -5i(-5) -5i(5i) \\ &= -20 +20i +25i +25 \\ &= \boxed{5 + 45i}.
\end{align*}

